e Two Dragon Pungs (6 points) if you get another J2.  \n\nDiscarding a single terminal like W9 seems safest\u2014it\u2019s isolated, hard to use, and only 1 left.  \n\nReason:  \nW9 is a terminal with only 1 copy left in the wall, making it unlikely to complete a meld. Keeping pairs (B9 and J2) maintains options for pung or pair. Discarding W9 preserves hand flexibility and avoids breaking potential scoring combinations like Dragon Pung.  \n\nAnswer: Play W9"}
